<Doc slug={slug} title="API keys">
  <h1>API keys</h1>
  <p>cortex selects a provider and model; axon reads endpoint configuration and credentials.</p>

  <h2>Provider settings</h2>
  <p>Place the provider definition in <code>~/.config/axon/axon.yaml</code>. Reference a variable rather than putting a key in YAML:</p>
  <pre><code>providers:
  openrouter:
    base_url: https://openrouter.ai/api
    api_key: &#36;&#123;OPENROUTER_API_KEY&#125;
    models:
      deepseek/deepseek-v3.2:</code></pre>
  <p>Put <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-key</code> in <code>~/.config/axon/.env</code> and set its permissions to <code>600</code> on Linux or macOS. The repository's <code>.env.example</code> is a template, not a credential file.</p>

  <h2>Local providers</h2>
  <p>A local Ollama endpoint can be configured without an API key. Give the provider a <code>base_url</code> and a model name in axon, then select them in cortex.</p>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
